Ukrainian law contains no offence of hitchhiking (''автостоп''), and on ordinary roads it is legal. [https://zakon.rada.gov.ua/laws/show/1306-2001-%D0%BF Clause 4.14(d) of the ''Правила дорожнього руху''] forbids a pedestrian to move along an ''автомагістраль'' or a ''дорога для автомобілів'' — but it names the exceptions in the same breath: footpaths, parking places and rest areas. That concedes more than most European codes do, because it means the ''майданчик для відпочинку'' and the motorway petrol station are places where you may lawfully stand and ask a driver. The carriageway, the hard shoulder and the slip road are not, so arrange to be dropped at a rest area rather than at the ramp. On every other road hitchhiking is unregulated: stand on the verge where a driver can see you and pull over safely.
